{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1210255-what-if-overwatch-blizzard-canon","id":1210255,"title":"What If? Overwatch (Blizzard) Canon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-22T20:24:45-07:00","id":1210255,"title":"What If? Overwatch (Blizzard) Canon","content":"Because I felt the need to complete the DCU and Marvel reimagining, and I know squat about Image. That, and the game already has a Gothic Horror event that happens every Halloween, so...<br /> <br /> What if the reason Overwatch's technology seems so much like magic was that...it was. Magic and advanced technology draw on the same laws of the universe in the CofD, so the world of Overwatch being what happens after humanity powers through the elementary sections of occult physics isn't that far fetched. That, and if you're someone who crawls through the lore a lot, you quickly realize that the supposed utopia...really isn't. See: Vishkar, and them reacting to discovering no evidence of wrongdoing by a competitor being to blow up their building rather than lose a construction bid.<br /> <br /> So, random theories on what various Overwatch Heroes are through a CofD lens?<br /> <br /> My personal picks:<br /> <br /> Tracer: Hungry Sin-Eater. Yeah, no lucky time-shift here, that accident left her very dead and joined with a geist personifying the risk of fatal accidents in stunts, giving her the distinct easy-going attitude.<br /> <br /> Symmetra: Obrimos Seer of the Throne trying very hard to convince herself she was recruited by the right side despite eying a phone number to the local thearchs' recruitment center.<br /> <br /> Roadhog: Hunter in Darkness Rahu, living embodiment trying to protect what's left of his home somehow. Sometimes not as effectively as he'd like.<br /> <br /> Widowmaker: Centimanus Tammuz made from the remains of Amelie Lacroix, and having some strong Residual Memories. It's not even that she wants to be evil, it's that she has no idea how other to be than an assassin. If she ever leaves Talon she'll be a good Pariah.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Realized that, given what she was made for, Tammuz fits Widowmaker more than Galateid. She is no one's companion, as evinced by that &quot;Under the Mistletoe&quot; highlight (she pulls it out to hang over her head...then punches the cameraman out in disgust).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-23-2018, 07:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T14:19:18-07:00","id":1210594,"title":"","content":"Others (ie, Talon, because bad guys are cool):<br /> <br /> Doomfist: Abnormally humanitarian Ivory Claw with a distinct Fetish containing a Strength spirit.<br /> <br /> Reaper: Deviant, Nemesis with a focus on his past as the thing he hates, considered a Devout due to his friendship with Moira.<br /> <br /> Sombra: Autumn Court Wizened who joined up with Talon to protect herself from her Keeper, on her way to becoming a Goblin Queen due to her abuse of Goblin Contracts to hide her identity and get everywhere in computer systems.<br /> <br /> Moira: Mysterium Thrysus-turned-Scelestus, chasing a Mystery that stats the Abyss and Supernal are the same thing through different lenses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T14:30:11-07:00","id":1210599,"title":"","content":"Likes aside, gotta give you credit for always coming up with creative and unexpected translations from one setting to the CotD, Leliel. Kudos, really.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T16:21:05-07:00","id":1210670,"title":"","content":"If Sombra isn't an Unchained, I'll eat one of my hats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's 